/*
:name: mod_general
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: mod_general.foo
:pyrope_top: foo
*/

// The GENERAL remainder cell (Ntype_op::Rem). These three shapes were HARD
// ERRORS in tolg until the op existed -- they were the `errors/`-tree tests
// mod_runtime_divisor, mod_unsupported and mod_signed_dividend, which asserted
// the absence of the feature and are replaced by this file.
//
// Putting the "can this be synthesized?" question in tolg made every other
// consumer pay for it: bitwidth, constprop, the LEC encoder and the simulator
// can all reason about `%` perfectly well, and only the netlist mapper cannot.
// The restriction now lives in pass.abc (diag `rem-unsupported`), so a design
// that merely CONTAINS a remainder compiles, simulates and verifies.
//
// SEMANTICS pinned here: TRUNCATED remainder, sign following the DIVIDEND, the
// same as Verilog `%`, Dlop::rem_op and cvc5 BITVECTOR_SREM. `rs` is the arm
// that would catch a floored/SMOD encoding -- a negative dividend is exactly
// where truncated and floored disagree, and it is invisible in the other two.
// There is ONE op and no unsigned flavour: every LNAST/LGraph value is signed
// and unsigned is just the non-negative subset.
pub comb foo(a:u8, b:u8, s:s8) -> (rr:u8, r5:u3, rs:s8) {
  rr = a % b     // RUNTIME divisor  (was `mod-runtime-divisor`)
  r5 = a % 5     // non-power-of-two (was `mod-unsupported-divisor`)
  rs = s % 8     // possibly-NEGATIVE dividend (was `mod-signed-dividend`)
}
